The ``full_name`` of an instrument, instrument module, ``ChannelTuple`` or parameter, and
thereby the ``name`` of an instrument, is now cached on first access. Resolving these names
walked up the chain of parent instruments on every access, which was a significant part of the
time spent taking a snapshot of a station, e.g. at the start of every measurement. Taking a
snapshot of a station with a few thousand parameters on nested instrument modules is now around
25% faster. The name is only cached if it is built by the default implementations of
``name_parts`` and ``short_name`` of the component and all its parents, since these only depend
on attributes set when the component is created. Components where any of these are overridden,
and therefore may change name after creation, still compute ``full_name`` on every access.
